      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the original test. I'll improve it by:\n1. Removing unused imports and helper methods (`basic()`, `isClosed()`, `getReader()`)\n2. Consolidating the redundant `seen` declaration/assignment\n3. Breaking the long HTML literal into readable chunks\n4. Adding a format comment to `trackSeen`\n5. Moving the assertion outside the try block and naming the expected stringThe improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports and helper methods, consolidates the `StringBuilder` declaration, breaks the long HTML literal into readable lines, adds a format comment to `trackSeen`, and separates the assertion with a named `expected` variable — all while preserving identical runtime behavior."
